What is printed?

```c
int g = 2;
switch (g) {
    case 1: printf("A");
    case 2: printf("B");
    case 3: printf("C"); break;
    default: printf("D");
}
```

What is printed?

```c
int a = -1, b = 5;
if (a > 0)
    if (b > 0) printf("X");
else printf("Y");
```

What does this do?

```c
int n = 3;
while (n > 0)
    printf("%d ", n);
    n = n - 1;
```

